      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m02_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "At $90^\\circ$, the dot product of $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is zero.",
        "The third coordinate contributes $-7p$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{OA}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{OB}=3(2)+(-6)(-6)+p(-7)=42-7p$.",
        "$42-7p=0$, so $p=6$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s17_11_q2_ii",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p3_t_vectors_m02_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Insert the value of $p$ from (i) and scale $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ to find $\\overrightarrow{OC}$.",
        "Subtract $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ to form $\\overrightarrow{BC}$, then normalize."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$\\overrightarrow{OC}=\\frac23(3,-6,6)=(2,-4,4)$ and $\\overrightarrow{BC}=\\overrightarrow{OC}-\\overrightarrow{OB}=(0,2,11)$.",
        "$|BC|=\\sqrt{0^2+2^2+11^2}=\\sqrt{125}$, so the required unit vector is $\\frac1{\\sqrt{125}}(0,2,11)$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
